  "structural_change": "hd4 (KV-AHUB 10-17): RA_RLY 0 -> 1 and PV_RLY 0 -> 1 (module defaults = the hardened config): the parent qkd_ahub_die hp4b gate measured the core S-face pb_ra -> pbst ra hop at ~700 um (setup -145 ps pre-route, -286 post-CTS) and pl_rz -> pvlg rz at ~600 um, both unregistered by the hd3 latency contract; the parent now registers both (AS +1: P path +1 edge, NPR unchanged). Same pins and outline. Previous: hd3 (Q-KVSYS-STRIP, VIS-ROM QKV-07 sev2): hd2 CLOSED but its N face carried the whole Z-head bus (1,345 pins at 8.9/um, half on M3) -> solid red GRT strip along N while the body was 56% empty (fill 0.185). The core now sits in the CENTRE of the hub parent's Z row (ahub parent kit qkd_ahub_die): heads 0/1 leave on the W face (zw_*, 672 pins, 4.4/um M4), heads 2/3 + the reciprocal leaf on the E face (ze_*, rc_*, 738, 4.9/um M4), the hub outputs on N (am/out/ev/fault, 673, 4.5/um), stack inputs + P.V tiles + beat-store address on S (857, 5.7/um M3+M5). Same RTL logic and flops (the Z ports are split by face only: zh_* are now internal registers wired to zw_*/ze_*), outline 151.2 kept (= the pbst/pvlg/zh footprint: one tile size in the hub). Bench qkd_ahub_d eq (3 relay configs x 3 seeds) exact, mutant FAIL.",
